# UI Components

Follow these rules for every Vue component and layout in this project.

## Layout Principles

- Use a single root element in every Vue SFC.
- Keep page components thin. Put app chrome, navigation, and shell structure in layouts, not in pages.
- Reuse the existing app shell pattern in `resources/js/layouts`, especially `AppLayout.vue`, instead of creating ad hoc wrappers.
- Build reusable UI in `resources/js/components` and keep page-specific markup inside `resources/js/pages`.
- Do not duplicate sidebars, headers, footers, or page containers across pages.

## Vue Conventions

- Use `<script setup lang="ts">` for new components unless there is a strong reason not to.
- Keep component props explicit and typed.
- Prefer small, focused components over large page files with deeply nested markup.
- Use semantic HTML elements such as `header`, `nav`, `main`, `aside`, and `footer` when building layout structure.
- Keep slot usage simple and predictable.

## Styling Rules

- Prefer Tailwind utility classes first.
- Keep global design tokens and base typography in `resources/css/app.css`.
- Avoid inline styles unless there is no practical Tailwind alternative.
- Use local `<style>` blocks only when the styling is truly component-specific and cannot be expressed cleanly with utilities.
- Keep responsive behavior mobile-first and add breakpoints intentionally.
- Avoid layout hacks that depend on brittle absolute positioning, high z-index values, or duplicated spacing rules.

## Navigation and Routing

- Use Inertia `Link` components for navigation.
- Use Wayfinder-generated helpers for route URLs and form actions.
- Do not hardcode URLs when a named route or generated helper exists.
- Keep links, buttons, and navigation items visually consistent across the app.

## Inertia and Page Structure

- Inertia pages should live in `resources/js/pages` and render through `Inertia::render()` on the backend.
- Layouts should own the shell; pages should own content.
- If a page needs a wrapper, prefer composition over copying shell markup.
- Keep loading, empty, and error states inside the page or component that owns the state.
- Do not mix server-side controller concerns into view components.

## Quality Bar

- Keep markup readable and easy to scan.
- Prefer explicit structure over clever abstractions.
- Match the existing design language in the repo before introducing new patterns.
- Do not add placeholder UI, lorem ipsum, or fake interactions.
